        "original_id": "fffa479c-e7ea-57ec-a2ff-bf61e1f39aac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Markus Feehily, Bobby Fuller\n- Organizations: Westlife, The Bobby Fuller Four\n- Products: Fire\n- Topics: music careers\n\nFacts:\n- Bobby Fuller was born on October 22, 1942, and he was an American rock singer, songwriter, and guitarist.\n- Bobby Fuller recorded \"Love's Made a Fool of You\" and a cover of \"I Fought the Law\" with his mid-1960s group The Bobby Fuller Four.\n- Bobby Fuller died on July 18, 1966.\n- Markus Feehily was born as Markus Michael Patrick Feehily on 28 May 1980, and he was formerly known as Mark Feehily.\n- Markus Feehily is an Irish singer and songwriter.\n- Markus Feehily was a vocalist in Westlife.\n- Fire is the debut solo studio album by Markus Feehily.",
